  "goodToKnow": "Das Porzellan is porcelain or china. In 1708 Johann Friedrich Böttger, working for Augustus the Strong in Saxony, helped discover how to make hard-paste porcelain, and Meissen became Europe's first porcelain factory in 1710; its crossed swords mark is still famous. Idioms: wie ein Elefant im Porzellanladen (like a bull in a china shop) and Porzellan zerschlagen (to do diplomatic damage). Stressed on the last syllable."
